␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀" Vim keymap file for Bulgarian and Russian characters, "bds" layout.
" Most of it can be used with both utf-8 and cp1251 file encodings, except
" the accented characters which can only be stored in utf-8.
" This file itself is in utf-8.

" Maintainer: Boyko Bantchev <boykobb@gmail.com>
" URI: http://www.math.bas.bg/bantchev/vim/bulgarian-bds.vim
" Last Changed: 2010 May 4

" This keymap corresponds to what is called Bulgarian standard typewriter
" keyboard layout, or "–ë–î–°".
"
" Note that, in addition to the Bulgarian alphabet, the BDS layout prescribes
" the presence of the following characters:
"     ‚Äî  The Russian letters —ã (small), and –≠ and —ç (capital and small).
"     ‚Äî  The latin capital letters I and V ‚Äì used to type Roman numerals
"        without having to leave Cyrillic mode.
"
" Some punctuation characters present in ascii are mapped in BDS to keys
" different from the ones they occupy in the QWERTY layout, because the latter
" keys are used to type other characters.
"
" In this keymap, also defined (besides BDS) are:
"     ‚Äî  The Russian letters –Å and —ë (capital and small), as well as the
"        Russian capital letter –´ (see above for the small counterpart).
"        This way, using the bulgarian-bds keymap, one can access both
"        the Bulgarian and the Russian alphabets.
"     ‚Äî  The quotation marks ‚Äû ‚Äú ‚Äù ‚Äò ‚Äô (used in the Bulgarian and English
"        quotation styles), as well as ¬´ ¬ª (Russian quotation style).
"     ‚Äî  The characters ¬ß, ‚Ññ, ‚Äì (en-dash), ‚Äî (em-dash), ‚Ä¶, ‚Ä¢, ¬∑, ¬±, ¬∞, ¬¨,
"        ¬§, ‚Ç¨, ‚Ä∞, ‚Ä†, ‚Ä°, and ¬∂.
"
" The keymap also defines key combinations for grave and acute accents.
" (Grave accent is used in Bulgarian, acute in Russian, but both accents
" apply to other languages as well.)
"
" For details of what key or key combination maps to what character, please
" see below the map itself.
"
" See also http://www.math.bas.bg/bantchev/vim/kbdbul.html (in Bulgarian).

scriptencoding utf-8

let b:keymap_name = "bds"

loadkeymap
D       –ê       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER A
?       –ë       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER BE
L       –í       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER VE
H       –ì       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER GHE
O       –î       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER DE
E       –ï       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER IE
E::     –Å       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER IO
G       –ñ       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER ZHE
P       –ó       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER ZE
R       –ò       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER I
X       –ô       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER SHORT I
U       –ö       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER KA
>       –õ       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER EL
:       –ú       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER EM
K       –ù       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER EN
F       –û       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER O
M       –ü       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER PE
<       –†       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER ER
I       –°       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER ES
J       –¢       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER TE
W       –£       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER U
B       –§       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER EF
N       –•       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER HA
{       –¶       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER TSE
\"      –ß       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER CHE
T       –®       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER SHA
Y       –©       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER SHCHA
C       –™       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER HARD SIGN
CX      –´       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER YERU
A       –¨       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER SOFT SIGN
V       –≠       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER REVERSED E
Z       –Æ       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER YU
S       –Ø       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER YA
d       –∞       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER A
\/      –±       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER BE
l       –≤       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER VE
h       –≥       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER GHE
o       –¥       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER DE
e       –µ       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER IE
e::     —ë       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER IO
g       –∂       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER ZHE
p       –∑       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER ZE
r       –∏       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER I
x       –π       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER SHORT I
u       –∫       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER KA
\.      –ª       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER EL
;       –º       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER EM
k       –Ω       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER EN
f       –æ       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER O
m       –ø       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER PE
,       —Ä       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER ER
i       —Å       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER ES
j       —Ç       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER TE
w       —É       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER U
b       —Ñ       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER EF
n       —Ö       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER HA
[       —Ü       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER TSE
'       —á       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER CHE
t       —à       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER SHA
y       —â       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER SHCHA
c       —ä       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER HARD SIGN
Q       —ã       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER YERU
a       —å       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER SOFT SIGN
v       —ç       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER REVERSED E
z       —é       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER YU
s       —è       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER YA
_       I       LATIN CAPITAL LETTER I
+       V       LATIN CAPITAL LETTER V
$       "       QUOTATION MARK
\\      (       LEFT PARENTHESIS
|       )       RIGHT PARENTHESIS
#       +       PLUS SIGN
q       ,       COMMA
(       -       HYPHEN-MINUS
=       .       FULL STOP (PERIOD)
*       /       SOLIDUS (SLASH)
&       :       COLON
]       ;       SEMICOLON
^       =       EQUALS SIGN
@       ?       QUESTION MARK
}       ¬ß       SECTION SIGN (PARAGRAPH SIGN)
)       ‚Ññ       NUMERO SIGN
--      ‚Äì       EN DASH
---     ‚Äî       EM DASH
..      ‚Ä¶       HORIZONTAL ELLIPSIS
``      ‚Äú       LEFT DOUBLE QUOTATION MARK
''      ‚Äù       RIGHT DOUBLE QUOTATION MARK
,,      ‚Äû       DOUBLE LOW-9 QUOTATION MARK
`.      ‚Äò       LEFT SINGLE QUOTATION MARK
'.      ‚Äô       RIGHT SINGLE QUOTATION MARK
<<      ¬´       LEFT-POINTING DOUBLE ANGLE QUOTATION MARK
>>      ¬ª       RIGHT-POINTING DOUBLE ANGLE QUOTATION MARK
**      ‚Ä¢       BULLET
,.      ¬∑       MIDDLE DOT      
+-      ¬±       PLUS-MINUS SIGN
^o      ¬∞       DEGREE SIGN
~~      ¬¨       NOT SIGN
@@      ¬§       CURRENCY SIGN
$$      ‚Ç¨       EURO SIGN
%%      ‚Ä∞       PER MILLE SIGN
+|      ‚Ä†       DAGGER
++      ‚Ä°       DOUBLE DAGGER
||      ¬∂       PILCROW SIGN

" Accented characters cannot map onto cp1251 ‚Äì use utf-8 file encoding.
" To apply an accent to a letter, type the corresponding key combination
" to the immediate right of that letter.
^`      <char-0x300>    COMBINING GRAVE ACCENT
^'      <char-0x301>    COMBINING ACUTE ACCENT
␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀" Vim keymap file for Bulgarian and Russian characters, "phonetic" layout.
" Most of it can be used with both utf-8 and cp1251 file encodings, except
" the accented vowels which can only be stored in utf-8.
" This file itself is in utf-8.

" Maintainer:   Boyko Bantchev <boykobb@gmail.com>
" URI: http://www.math.bas.bg/bantchev/vim/bulgarian-phonetic.vim
" Last Changed: 2010 May 4

" This keymap corresponds to what is called "phonetic layout" in Bulgaria:
" Cyrillic letters tend to be mapped to their Latin homophones wherever
" there are ones.  Most keys corresponding to punctuation characters are
" left unmapped, so they retain their usual (QWERTY) meanings when typing
" Cyrillic.
"
" In addition to the Bulgarian alphabet, the keymap makes accessible the
" following characters:
"     ‚Äî  The letters –Å and —ë, –≠ and —ç, and –´ and —ã (in pairs of capital and
"        small).  These are the letters in the Russian alphabet that are not
"        present in Bulgarian, so using the bulgarian-phonetic keymap one can
"        type in Russian, too.
"     ‚Äî  The quotation marks ‚Äû ‚Äú ‚Äù ‚Äò ‚Äô (used in the Bulgarian and English
"        quotation styles), as well as ¬´ ¬ª (Russian quotation style).
"     ‚Äî  The characters ¬ß, ‚Ññ, ‚Äì (en-dash), ‚Äî (em-dash), ‚Ä¶, ‚Ä¢, ¬∑, ¬±, ¬∞, ¬¨,
"        ¬§, ‚Ç¨, ‚Ä∞, ‚Ä†, ‚Ä°, and ¬∂.
"
" The keymap also defines key combinations for grave and acute accents.
" (Grave accent is used in Bulgarian, acute in Russian, but both accents
" apply to other languages as well.)
"
" For details of what key or key combination maps to what character, please
" see below the map itself.
"
" See also http://www.math.bas.bg/bantchev/vim/kbdbul.html (in Bulgarian).

scriptencoding utf-8

let b:keymap_name = "pho"

loadkeymap
A       –ê       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER A
B       –ë       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER BE
W       –í       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER VE
G       –ì       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER GHE
D       –î       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER DE
E       –ï       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER IE
E::     –Å       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER IO
V       –ñ       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER ZHE
Z       –ó       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER ZE
I       –ò       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER I
J       –ô       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER SHORT I
K       –ö       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER KA
L       –õ       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER EL
M       –ú       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER EM
N       –ù       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER EN
O       –û       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER O
P       –ü       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER PE
R       –†       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER ER
S       –°       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER ES
T       –¢       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER TE
U       –£       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER U
F       –§       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER EF
H       –•       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER HA
C       –¶       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER TSE
~       –ß       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER CHE
{       –®       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER SHA
}       –©       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER SHCHA
Y       –™       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER HARD SIGN
YI      –´       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER YERU
X       –¨       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER SOFT SIGN
YE      –≠       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER REVERSED E
|       –Æ       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER YU
Q       –Ø       CYRILLIC CAPITAL LETTER YA
a       –∞       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER A
b       –±       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER BE
w       –≤       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER VE
g       –≥       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER GHE
d       –¥       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER DE
e       –µ       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER IE
e::     —ë       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER IO
v       –∂       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER ZHE
z       –∑       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER ZE
i       –∏       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER I
j       –π       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER SHORT I
k       –∫       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER KA
l       –ª       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER EL
m       –º       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER EM
n       –Ω       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER EN
o       –æ       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER O
p       –ø       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER PE
r       —Ä       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER ER
s       —Å       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER ES
t       —Ç       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER TE
u       —É       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER U
f       —Ñ       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER EF
h       —Ö       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER HA
c       —Ü       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER TSE
`       —á       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER CHE
[       —à       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER SHA
]       —â       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER SHCHA
y       —ä       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER HARD SIGN
yi      —ã       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER YERU
x       —å       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER SOFT SIGN
ye      —ç       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER REVERSED E
\\      —é       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER YU
q       —è       CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER YA
!!      ¬ß       SECTION SIGN (PARAGRAPH SIGN)
##      ‚Ññ       NUMERO SIGN
--      ‚Äì       EN DASH
---     ‚Äî       EM DASH
..      ‚Ä¶       HORIZONTAL ELLIPSIS
``      ‚Äú       LEFT DOUBLE QUOTATION  MARK
''      ‚Äù       RIGHT DOUBLE QUOTATION MARK
,,      ‚Äû       DOUBLE LOW-9 QUOTATION MARK
`.      ‚Äò       LEFT SINGLE QUOTATION MARK
'.      ‚Äô       RIGHT SINGLE QUOTATION MARK
<<      ¬´       LEFT-POINTING DOUBLE ANGLE QUOTATION MARK
>>      ¬ª       RIGHT-POINTING DOUBLE ANGLE QUOTATION MARK
**      ‚Ä¢       BULLET
,.      ¬∑       MIDDLE DOT      
+-      ¬±       PLUS-MINUS SIGN
^o      ¬∞       DEGREE SIGN
~~      ¬¨       NOT SIGN
@@      ¬§       CURRENCY SIGN
$$      ‚Ç¨       EURO SIGN
%%      ‚Ä∞       PER MILLE SIGN
+|      ‚Ä†       DAGGER
++      ‚Ä°       DOUBLE DAGGER
||      ¬∂       PILCROW SIGN

" Accented characters cannot map onto cp1251 ‚Äì use utf-8 file encoding.
" To apply an accent to a letter, type the corresponding key combination
" to the immediate right of that letter.
^`      <char-0x300>    COMBINING GRAVE ACCENT
^'      <char-0x301>    COMBINING ACUTE ACCENT
